1
00:02:43,209 --> 00:02:47,385
<v DIRECTOR> Good morning. Welcome to the Early Learning Childcare Centre. How may I help you?

2
00:02:47,385 --> 00:02:51,151
<v CAROL> Hi. I spoke to you last week about enrolling my daughter to next year.

3
00:02:51,151 --> 00:02:56,655
<v DIRECTOR> Oh, yes. I’ll just get some details from you. So, you’re her mother?

4
00:02:56,655 --> 00:02:57,433
<v CAROL> That’s right.

5
00:02:57,433 --> 00:02:58,775
<v DIRECTOR> And, can I have your name?

6
00:02:58,775 --> 00:03:00,950
<v CAROL> It’s Carol, Carol Smith.

7
00:03:00,950 --> 00:03:02,899
<v DIRECTOR> And your daughter’s name?

8
00:03:02,899 --> 00:03:03,998
<v CAROL> It’s Kate.

9
00:03:03,998 --> 00:03:12,003
<v DIRECTOR> Now, we have several groups at the centre and we cater for children from three to five years old. How old is your daughter?

10
00:03:12,003 --> 00:03:15,451
<v CAROL> She’s three now but she turns four next month.

11
00:03:15,451 --> 00:03:19,491
<v DIRECTOR> I’ll put four down because that’s how old she’ll be when she starts.

12
00:03:19,491 --> 00:03:23,859
<v CAROL> Fine, she’s so excited about her birthday and coming to the centre.

13
00:03:23,859 --> 00:03:27,052
<v DIRECTOR> That’s good to hear. And what’s your address?

14
00:03:27,052 --> 00:03:37,042
<v CAROL> It’s 46 Wombat Road, that’s W-O-M-B-A-T. Woodside 4032.

15
00:03:37,042 --> 00:03:38,865
<v DIRECTOR> And what’s the phone number?

16
00:03:38,865 --> 00:03:45,017
<v CAROL> Oh … it’s … 3345 9865.

17
00:03:45,017 --> 00:03:49,331
<v DIRECTOR> So, have you decided on the days you’d like to bring your daughter here?

18
00:03:49,331 --> 00:03:52,531
<v CAROL> I’d prefer Monday and Wednesday if possible.

19
00:03:52,531 --> 00:04:08,482
<v DIRECTOR> Mmm. I’ll check, Monday’s fine, but I think the centre is already full for Wednesday. Erm. Yes. Sorry. It seems to be a very popular day. We can offer you a Thursday or a Friday as well.

20
00:04:08,482 --> 00:04:14,336
<v CAROL> Oh dear. I suppose Thursday would be all right because she has swimming on Friday.

21
00:04:14,336 --> 00:04:28,061
<v DIRECTOR> OK, got that. Because a lot of parents work, we do offer flexible start and finish times. We are open from 7:30 in the morning until 6 o’clock at night. What time would you like your daughter to start?

22
00:04:28,061 --> 00:04:37,205
<v CAROL> I need to get to work in the city by 9:00 so I’ll drop her off at 8:30. You’re pretty close to the city here so that should give me plenty of time to get there.

23
00:04:37,205 --> 00:04:54,475
<v DIRECTOR> That’s fine. Now, we also need to decide which group she’ll be in. we have two different groups and they’re divided up according to age. There’s the green group. Which is for three- to four-year-olds. And then there’s the red group which is for four- to five-year-olds.

24
00:04:54,475 --> 00:04:59,156
<v CAROL> She’s quite mature for her age and she can already write her name and read a little.

25
00:04:59,156 --> 00:05:04,703
<v DIRECTOR> Well, I’ll put her in the red group and we can always change her to the green one if there are any problems.

26
00:05:04,703 --> 00:05:06,266
<v CAROL> That sounds fine.

27
00:05:06,266 --> 00:05:17,493
<v DIRECTOR> OK. Let’s move on to meals. We can provide breakfast, lunch and dinner. As she’s finishing pretty early, she won’t need dinner, will you give her breakfast before she comes?

28
00:05:17,493 --> 00:05:19,522
<v CAROL> Yes, she’ll only need lunch.

29
00:06:07,185 --> 00:06:14,172
<v DIRECTOR> Now, does she have any medical conditions we need to know about? Does she have asthma or any hearing problems for example?

30
00:06:14,172 --> 00:06:17,070
<v CAROL> No. But she does need to wear glasses.

31
00:06:17,070 --> 00:06:18,994
<v DIRECTOR> Oh, I’ll make a note of that.

32
00:06:18,994 --> 00:06:22,749
<v CAROL> Yes, she’s pretty good about wearing them, she can’t see much without them.

33
00:06:22,749 --> 00:06:27,884
<v DIRECTOR> Right. OK. Now, I also need emergency contact details.

34
00:06:27,884 --> 00:06:30,398
<v CAROL> So what sort of information do you need?

35
00:06:30,398 --> 00:06:37,013
<v DIRECTOR> Just the name and number of a friend or family member we can contact in case we can’t get hold of you at any time.

36
00:06:37,013 --> 00:06:50,224
<v CAROL> OK. That’d better be my sister … Jenny Ball. That’s B-A-double L. Her phone number is 3346 7523.

37
00:06:50,224 --> 00:06:53,300
<v DIRECTOR> Great. So she is the child’s aunt?

38
00:06:53,300 --> 00:06:54,847
<v CAROL> Yes, that’s right.

39
00:06:54,847 --> 00:06:59,790
<v DIRECTOR> I’ll make a note of that as well. Now, is there anything you’d like to ask?

40
00:06:59,790 --> 00:07:03,480
<v CAROL> What about payment? How much are the fees each term?

41
00:07:03,480 --> 00:07:10,795
<v DIRECTOR> Well, for two days and the hours you’ve chosen, that will be $450 altogether.

42
00:07:10,795 --> 00:07:13,866
<v CAROL> OK, and do I have to pay that now?

43
00:07:13,866 --> 00:07:24,602
<v DIRECTOR> No, we send out invoices once the children start at the centre. You can choose to pay at the end of each term or we do offer a slightly discounted rate if you pay every month.

44
00:07:24,602 --> 00:07:30,861
<v CAROL> Oh, I’ll do that then. I find it easier to budget that way and I’m not used to the term dates just yet.

45
00:07:30,861 --> 00:07:37,495
<v DIRECTOR> Good, it makes it a lot simpler for us as well. Well, that’s everything. Would you like me to show you around …?